    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96760.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 26,
    "turn_text": "Can you push that? Yes, I think that happened. Here's what I think we can do. There is a growing consensus among the best people in the country across the board and all of the disciplines that relate to the fight against cancer that we should have a common language. Like, for example, when the human genome was sequenced, we found out that, you know, you're talking about a couple billion pieces of information and thousands of genes and it was so big that we concluded no one outfit could do it. So what we did is we went around the world literally And we handed out, we said, okay, you take, I'm being figurative, you take A to C, and you take C to P, and we broke it up. But the condition was that each of these organizations, and some were in other countries, had to immediately share all of the data that they got with one another. It was insistent by the NIH that had to be done that way. So we cracked the human genome. We actually were able to do that in sharing that information instantaneously. And now in the human genome, there is a common language. You must use the precise language that is needed the precise terminology in order to do anything in terms of dealing with the genome. There is no such precise language as it relates to medical records. So one, to oversimplify it, one doc will write down a broken leg. The other guy will write down a broken femur. Another guy will write down a fracture tip. And there's no way the computer can go out and aggregate all that data. So one of the things I proposed when I started this five months ago is why don't we insist on a common language and electronic record keeping? Well, that made a lot of people very angry. But at the last moonshot where we had over 9,000 people participating, you had leading members of industry and medicine saying, we need a common language. And that's one of the things I talk to one of the brightest guys that are met is Lander.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
